      %a{href: "#{asset_prefix}#{lang_dir}hardware/"}= nav_hardware
      %a{href: "#{asset_prefix}#{lang_dir}documentation/", class: "active"}= nav_documentation
    %main.sub-main
      .sub-content
        %h1= budget_h1
        %p.sub-lead= budget_lead

        %h2= budget_h2_flash
        %p
          The 1&nbsp;MB ESP8285 flash is dominated by the <strong>WebUI</strong>: the bundled client build is ~160&nbsp;KB compressed (~16% of flash) after tree-shaking. The float runtime (<code>_scanf_float</code>, <code>_printf_float</code>, <code>_dtoa_r</code>, <code>_strtod_l</code> …) is ~9.7&nbsp;KB — real but not the biggest lever. Current baseline sits at ~68.6% flash; the 60% target needs a ~83&nbsp;KB cut, and the WebUI is the only lever large enough to reach it.

        %h2= budget_h2_ram
        %p
          The ESP8285 exposes roughly <strong>23&nbsp;KB of heap</strong>. Config saves must never allocate a big JSON document on the heap — the ornithopter config saver streams directly to LittleFS to avoid exhausting the heap and rebooting mid-poll. Keep <code>DynamicJsonDocument</code> out of the hot path; prefer stack buffers and direct writes.

        %h2= budget_h2_tips
        %ul
          %li Tree-shake unused ELRS-RX pages from the WebUI bundle.
          %li Avoid <code>String</code> concatenation in loops — it fragments the heap.
          %li Stream JSON to LittleFS with <code>File::print</code> instead of building documents.
          %li Keep float formatting out of the telemetry hot path (pre-scaled integers).
          %li Prefer <code>#ifdef</code>-gated modules (Zephyrus compiles to no-ops when absent).

        %h2= budget_h2_targets
        %table
          %tr
            %th Target
            %th Flash budget
            %th RAM budget
          %tr
            %td PteronautOS_ESP8285_2400_RX
            %td ≤ 60%
            %td ≤ 65%
        %p
          The manifest forbids exceeding <strong>60% flash / 65% RAM</strong> to leave margin for expansion. Measure after every feature; a green build is not a live build until it is flashed and its boot log read.

